  <page_number>93</page_number>
  <running_head>VARIA POEMATA.</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">POCILLI DONVM,</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="2" para="true">EIDEM.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">DOstarum[?] potis Elegantiarum</l>
    <l n="4">Beza magnificas referre laudes,</l>
    <l n="5">Pocillum artificis fagaciore</l>
    <l n="6">Mitto Dædalei[?] manu politum:</l>
    <l n="7">Vicinique tui fauente torno.</l>
    <l n="8">Quod vix excipiat cauo pusillo</l>
    <l n="9">Flentis lachrymulam unicam puelli.</l>
    <l n="10">Quod vix ventriculo queat minuto</l>
    <l n="11">Roris exiguam tenere guttam.</l>
    <l n="12">Quo formica suam labore fessa</l>
    <l n="13">Iugi parvula vix sitim levarit.</l>
    <l n="14">Quo nec florilega fagax proboscis</l>
    <l n="15">Mergi posset apis calente sole:</l>
    <l n="16">Nec arguta femel cicada siccas</l>
    <l n="17">Cantu perpetuo rigare fauces.</l>
    <l n="18">Vix illo valeat culex iacere,</l>
    <l n="19">Aut pulex tenuis latere totus.</l>
    <l n="20">O si tam modicis, minutulisque</l>
    <l n="21">Pauxillo madidis mero cululis</l>
    <l n="22">Decertare modo iuuaret acres</l>
    <l n="23">Potores: neque poculo liceret</l>
    <l n="24">Provocare viros capaciore!</l>
    <l n="25">Laudarent Sapido politiores</l>
    <l n="26">Vates Teutonici fuos: nec unquam</l>
    <l n="27">Tam charis biberent merum popinis.</l>
    <l n="28" para="true">I. I.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>DOstarum: the initial word is doubtful; the long-s form could be read several ways, so it is marked [?]. Dædalei: the diphthong is partly obscured in the scan and is marked [?]. Beza: printed with a ligature-like form on the z. Signature "I. I." is printed at the foot right, with an ornament beside it, not transcribed.</notes>
</page>
